 donce's house, should graze one's cattle on the green crops in his fields, should harvest the ripe crops in his fields, should crush his sugar-cane, should accept rocikā and ciṭolā from him, should take stools, seats and cots from him and should take wood, fuel, grass, chaff, etc., from him’. For gṛh-āvataraṇa, see umbara-bheda. Words like rocikā, ciṭolā, etc., are not intelligible, although they certainly refer to certain obligations or levies. Cf. Ind. Ep., p. 394.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}]}